+
+### Bug fix: em dashes removed from all player-facing text (patch 0388)
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Bug Fix
+
+- Fixed a stray em dash appearing in the Statistics tab before any quests have been run
+```
+
+Full pass across `src/` and `electron/` for em dashes (`—`, U+2014) in
+text a player could actually see, following up on a general "no em
+dashes in player-facing copy" ask.
+
+**Audit method.** Walked every `.ts`/`.tsx` file the renderer and
+Electron main process ship, plus every quest/event/item JSON under
+`src/game/data/json/` (all already clean), plus `index.html` and
+`app.css` (also clean). Every other em dash found across the codebase
+lives in `/** ... */` or `//` code comments -- developer-facing prose
+explaining a formula or a past decision, never rendered to a player --
+and was deliberately left alone; touching those isn't part of this ask
+and they don't reach the game window.
+
+**The one real hit (`StatsPanel.tsx`):** the Statistics tab's success-
+rate line falls back to a bare `'—'` when `stats.totalQuests` is still
+`0` (a fresh guild, before any quest has resolved). Changed to `'N/A'`,
+matching how "no data yet" already reads elsewhere in the UI rather
+than introducing a new placeholder convention.
+
+**Docs (`README.md`, `WORKFLOW.md`, `SETUP-WINDOWS.md`, `DEVTOOL.md`,
+`QUEST-CHAINS.md`, `world-lore-pantheon.md`,
+`guild-idler-project-brief.md`, `content-drop-green-tide.md`,
+`guild-idler-status.md` itself) were left untouched on purpose --
+none of them ship inside the game and none are player-facing.
+
+**Verified:** `npx tsc --noEmit` passes clean. Re-ran the same audit
+grep after the edit -- zero em dashes remain outside comments and
+non-shipping markdown.
